<Docs title="Settings">
  <h1>Settings</h1>
  <p>
    MixRestore's settings let you customize scanning behavior and project management.
  </p>

  <h2>Scan directories</h2>
  <p>
    Configure which directories MixRestore searches when scanning for projects.
    By default, it looks in common Ableton project locations:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>~/Music/Ableton</code></li>
    <li><code>~/Documents</code></li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You can add or remove directories from the scan list in Settings. MixRestore searches
    recursively within each directory for <code>.als</code> files.
  </p>

  <h2>Ignored paths</h2>
  <p>
    If certain folders contain Ableton projects you don't want to track (e.g., tutorial
    files or archived work), add them to the ignored paths list. They won't appear in
    scan results.
  </p>

  <h2>Ignored files (Git)</h2>
  <p>
    Each tracked project has a <code>.gitignore</code> file that controls which files
    are excluded from version tracking. By default, MixRestore ignores:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>Backup/</code> — Ableton's automatic backup folder</li>
    <li><code>*.undo</code> — Undo history files</li>
    <li>OS files like <code>.DS_Store</code></li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You can customize the <code>.gitignore</code> to exclude large sample folders
    or other files you don't need versioned.
  </p>
</Docs>
